<h2>Understanding bonus terms before you claim</h2>
<p>A welcome bonus headline figure tells you very little without the conditions attached to it. The terms below are what actually decide whether a bonus is worth taking for your style of play.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Term</th>
<th>What it means</th>
<th>What to check</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Wagering requirement</td>
<td>Total stakes needed before withdrawing bonus-derived funds</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Game contribution</td>
<td>The percentage each game type counts toward wagering</td>
<td>Pokies usually contribute 100%; table games often contribute 10% or less</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Maximum bet while wagering</td>
<td>A stake cap enforced until wagering is cleared</td>
<td>Exceeding it can void bonus funds entirely</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Expiry / time limit</td>
<td>Window to complete all wagering</td>
<td>Shorter windows make large bonuses harder to clear realistically</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Maximum cashout / conversion cap</td>
<td>The most you can withdraw from bonus winnings</td>
<td>A low cap can make a large headline offer far less valuable</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h2>Games available at Australian online casinos</h2>
<p>The casinos on this page cover the main categories that Australian players look for. Here is how those categories break down in practice:</p>
<ul>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><strong>AUD accounts</strong> — look for sites that hold your balance in Australian dollars. Accounts denominated in another currency (such as euros or USD) expose you to conversion costs on every deposit and withdrawal.</li>
<li><strong>KYC (Know Your Customer) requirements</strong> — expect to submit proof of identity (passport or driver's licence) and proof of address before any payout is approved. Submitting these documents early avoids delays when you are ready to withdraw.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Additional products at these casino sites</h2>
<h2>Legal standing and eligibility for Australian players</h2>
<p><strong>Eligibility requirements:</strong> you must be aged 18 or over to open an account at any casino listed here. Operators will verify your age as part of the KYC process. Some casinos may restrict access based on country of residence beyond the basic age check; confirm your eligibility during registration.</p>
